@startuml
!include style/ail.puml
allowmixing
title G11b · The description layer: recording the calls and reaching their code
top to bottom direction
hide circle
hide empty methods
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45

$package(description, "The published description\nWatch declarations and contracts (G11a)\nStated API subset and release\nDependencies and supported configurations")
class "Writers, checkers and users" as agreement #EAF2F8 {
  Writers supply the required facts
  Checkers establish completeness and consistency
  Users retain access to the same contracts
}
class "Operations and their values (G11a)" as operations #EAF2F8 {
  watch_open · watch_view · watch_close
}
class "Reaching the code" as access #E8F3EB {
  An access path connects an operation to code
  A mapping accounts for its inputs and outputs
  Compatibility states when representations agree
}
$catalogue(definitions, "Selected machine-level definitions\nValue representations\nCalling rules and runtime facilities")

agreement -down-> description : carry the same facts\nthrough publication and use
description -down-> operations : describes these operations\nand their obligations
operations -down-> access : has a path to\nits implementation
access -right-> definitions : selects the rules\nfor crossing the boundary

legend bottom
  Folder = package; boxes = related facts; cylinder = shared definitions.
  Labelled arrows show description and access relations, not native calls.
  G11a expands the call facts; G1 expands the publication workflow.
  Checking a description needs complete, consistent facts.
  Establishing library behaviour needs separate implementation evidence.
  No complete access mapping for the watch header is supplied here.
  Non-normative overview; proposed tools remain future work.
endlegend
@enduml
